# Line-ending policy.
#
# This host has core.autocrlf=true. Git therefore rewrites LF -> CRLF on every
# checkout, worktree add, stash and stash pop. For most files that is harmless.
# For .planning/ it is not, and the failure is SILENT.
#
# GSD's frontmatter reader (get-shit-done/bin/lib/frontmatter.cjs) is a
# hand-rolled line parser, not a YAML parser, and it does not strip \r.
# Measured on this repo, same bytes, only the line endings differing:
#
#   01-26-PLAN.md as LF    -> {"all_passed": false, "passed": 0, "total": 5}
#   01-26-PLAN.md as CRLF  -> {"error": "No must_haves.artifacts found in frontmatter"}
#
# That is not a failing gate. It is NO gate — every artifact check and key-link
# check in the plan silently stops existing, and an executor can read the error
# as "nothing to verify" and proceed. It is the same class as a trailing '#'
# comment on a value line making the parser emit `undefined` so verify.cjs skips
# the check, which cost this phase two full red-team rounds to find.
#
# Pinning LF here is the permanent fix: it survives a fresh clone, a worktree,
# and anyone else's autocrlf setting.
.planning/** text eol=lf

# The repo's own tooling parses these with hand-rolled or line-oriented readers
# too (test/ci-config.test.cjs, test/repo-claims.test.cjs, the shim templates in
# src/main/hive.ts). Keep them LF for the same reason.
*.md        text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.cjs       text eol=lf
*.ts        text eol=lf
*.tsx       text eol=lf
*.json      text eol=lf
*.css       text eol=lf
*.html      text eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.gif       binary
*.ico       binary
*.woff      binary
*.woff2     binary
*.ttf       binary
*.node      binary
*.asar      binary
*.exe       binary
*.dll       binary
*.tmj       text eol=lf
